# Keep every text file at LF in the repository *and* in the working tree.
#
# Why: the formatter check (`oxfmt --check`, part of `bun check`) compares raw
# bytes. On Windows, Git's default `core.autocrlf=true` checks text files out
# with CRLF, which makes `oxfmt --check` report every file as misformatted —
# on this checkout that was 587 of 588 files, so the repository's own quality
# gate could never pass. Declaring `eol=lf` here overrides `core.autocrlf` for
# this repository, so `git checkout` writes LF on every platform and the check
# is meaningful again, with no need for `oxfmt --write` to rewrite the tree.
#
# Also normalizes existing CRLF content on the next `git add`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
